Z||000007||mrfixit58||08-23-2001||03:37 PM||||I think the ZR-1 scoop is about the nicest hood scoop around. But, if your thinking of installing it for extra cooling, I don't think it'll help except at idle. The base of the windsheld is a high pressure point. This means, with that scoop, air is forced "IN" at speed, not out. <P>This is why they were installed in the first place. The breather/carb was sealed to the bottom of the hood and the cowl provided freash cool air to the motor. <P>I just installed a steel cowl hood on my 97 Chevrolet pick-up and I can tell you for a FACT, air go into the scoop, not out. That is evident when you see the leaves sucked up to the scoops screen while moving.<P>Still it's real purty  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Roy :D<BR>87 GT   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG"> ||||reg||1
